I, Duke of Guise and Catherine of Cleves."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9:d02", "start": 191, "end": 289, "text": "His ecclesiastical post was entirely a sinecure; he was never ordained, and led a dissipated life."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9:d02", "start": 290, "end": 394, "text": "Nevertheless, he was made Archbishop of Reims in January 1605, and created cardinal on December 2, 1615."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9:d02", "start": 395, "end": 491, "text": "He incurred the displeasure of Louis XIII of France, and was imprisoned in the Bastille in 1620."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9:d02", "start": 492, "end": 567, "text": "However, he joined the royal campaign in Poitou in 1621, and there fell ill"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9:d03", "start": 0, "end": 180, "text": "Louis II, Cardinal of Guise Louis II, Cardinal of Guise (6 July 1555, Dampierre – 24 December 1588, Château de Blois), was the third son of Francis, Duke of Guise, and Anna d'Este."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9:d03", "start": 181, "end": 264, "text": "He was elected archbishop of Reims in 1574, succeeding his uncle, Charles of Guise."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9:d03", "start": 265, "end": 400, "text": "On 21 February 1578, he was created cardinal; he took the title of Cardinal of Guise, succeeding his uncle, Louis I, Cardinal of Guise."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9:d03", "start": 401, "end": 515, "text": "He was later named papal legate to Avignon, and made by Henry III of France a knight of the Order of Saint Esprit."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9:d03", "start": 516, "end": 546, "text": "His dedication to the cause of"}, "D5S1": {"document_number